c76df02b","type":"message","user":"U06ECBRTJ","text":"まぁ、そうなんですが…","ts":"1629081217.169100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"cEU"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3190a70b-85ef-4e9d-9bda-9834291b0973","type":"message","user":"U03C71D7H","text":"こういう時何も考えずに for を書くのが Go 言語かと思っていたが","ts":"1629081012.168900","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"euJs8"}]},{"client_msg_id":"DD81F3E1-2CAD-47FB-92A0-A09C6F80EF57","type":"message","user":"UKHUVMBJR","text":"たまに困るやつ。\ngenerics 待ちですね","ts":"1629080486.168500","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"v/pCA"}]},{"client_msg_id":"3C458CF0-58DE-4715-82F8-66536E89FC31","type":"message","user":"UFYACJ537","text":"これを待つ他ない… \u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/47649|https://github.com/golang/go/issues/47649\u003e","ts":"1629080481.168200","attachments":[{"color":"36a64f","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/47649|#47649 proposal: maps: new package to provide generic map functions\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/47649|#47649 proposal: maps: new package to provide generic map functions\u003e","text":"*Discussed in \u003chttps://github.com/golang/go/discussions/47330|golang/go#47330\u003e*\n\nOriginally posted by *ianlancetaylor* July 21, 2021  \nThis is a discussion that is intended to turn into a proposal.\n\nThis proposal is for use with #43651. We propose defining a new package, maps, that will provide functions that may be used with maps of any type. If this proposal is accepted, the new package will be included with the first release of Go that implements #43651 (we currently expect that that will be Go 1.18).\n\nThis description below is focused on the API, not the implementation. In general the implementation will be straightforward.\n\nSee also the slices proposal at #45955 (discussion at #47203).\n\n```\n// Package maps defines various functions useful with maps of any type.\npackage maps\n\n// Keys returns the keys of the map m.\n// The keys will be an indeterminate order.\nfunc Keys[K comparable, V any](m map[K]V) []K\n\n// Values returns the values of the map m.\n// The values will be in an indeterminate order.\nfunc Values[K comparable, V any](m map[K]V) []V\n\n// Equal reports whether two maps contain the same key/value pairs.\n// Values are compared using ==.\nfunc Equal[K, V comparable](m1, m2 map[K]V) bool\n\n// EqualFunc is like Equal, but compares values using cmp.\n// Keys are still compared with ==.\nfunc EqualFunc[K comparable, V1, V2 any](m1 map[K]V1, m2 map[K]V2, cmp func(V1, V2) bool) bool\n\n// Clear removes all entries from m, leaving it empty.\nfunc Clear[K comparable, V any](m map[K]V)\n\n// Clone returns a copy of m.  This is a shallow clone:\n// the new keys and values are set using ordinary assignment.\nfunc Clone[K comparable, V any](m map[K]V) map[K]V\n\n// Add adds all key/value pairs in src to dst. When a key in src\n// is already present in dst, the value in dst will be overwritten\n// by the value associated with the key in src.\nfunc Add[K comparable, V any](dst, src map[K]V)\n\n// Filter deletes any key/value pairs from m for which keep returns false.\nfunc Filter[K comparable, V any](m map[K]V, keep func(K, V) bool)\n```","fields":[{"title":"Labels","value":"Proposal, generics","short":true},{"title":"Comments","value":"5","short":true}],"mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/golang/go|golang/go\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png","ts":1628702019}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"U6pF"}]},{"client_msg_id":"0a513d4a-b504-4121-a103-cd64d46e87ac","type":"message","user":"U06ECBRTJ","text":"うーん…","ts":"1629080258.167400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_orig